
# Python bytecode
node_modules/
nn/.engine-cache.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local archive created by the Elo calibration reset. Keep the evidence locally,
# but do not push the old mixed-semantics rating state back into the live branch.
nn/elo-archive/

# Gauntlet runs: a frozen copy of the candidate plus that run's results. Freezing is the point --
# nn/medals/*.json are aliases publish-medals.js overwrites and re-pushes every cycle, so a long
# run has to play a copy or it can finish against a different model than it started with -- but
# that copy is a ~900KB weight blob per run, and the results are local evidence about one decision,
# not source. Kept out of the branch the trainer pushes to on its own.
nn/gauntlet-runs/

# This machine's name, used to file its medals under nn/medals/<machine>/ so several trainers on one
# branch accumulate instead of overwriting each other's three fixed filenames. It is the one file
# that MUST differ between clones -- committing it would hand every machine the same identity and
# rebuild the collision it exists to remove.
nn/.machine-id
